cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CRISPR Designer — trained sgRNA efficiency scorers with measured baselines"
abstract: >-
  A multi-organism CRISPR-Cas9 sgRNA designer where two trained efficiency
  scorers (a 200k-parameter encoder-only transformer and an XGBoost
  reproduction of Rule Set 2) are evaluated head-to-head on identical
  splits against the published Doench 2016 mammalian and crisprHAL E. coli
  corpora. The transformer ties XGBoost on mammalian data (Spearman ρ
  0.420 vs 0.459, overlapping 95% CIs) and loses cleanly on bacterial data
  (Spearman ρ 0.544 vs 0.626, non-overlapping CIs). Cross-kingdom transfer
  learning produced no improvement, suggesting CRISPR efficiency signal is
  largely organism-specific at the model scale tested.
